WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:19.572
"Oh no," Patrick thought, staring in dismay at Mickey's catcher's mitt.

2
00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:24.418
Daniel had just told Patrick that Coach rarely started seventh-graders like Patrick.

3
00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:29.979
This kid—an eighth-grader—would probably bump Patrick down to a backup catcher.

4
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.089
"There goes my fantastic baseball season," thought Patrick gloomily.

5
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:40.569
Just then Coach approached the dugout, his gray hair tucked under a Dragons cap.

6
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:45.813
"I see you two have met," he said.

7
00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:49.233
"Daniel's gonna coach the pitchers and catchers this year.

8
00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:55.227
I just informed him that he's got a new player. We're glad you moved here, Mickey," Coach added.

9
00:00:55.228 --> 00:00:58.322
"We need a good relief catcher."

10
00:00:58.323 --> 00:01:06.324
"Phew!" Patrick thought. Coach had just called Mickey a "relief" catcher. That had to mean that Coach thought of Patrick as starter.

11
00:01:06.325 --> 00:01:12.317
Coach jerked a thumb toward the field. "Get out there, you two. Daniel's waiting for you."

12
00:01:12.318 --> 00:01:17.942
After warm-ups, practice went into full swing. Patrick crouched behind the plate.

13
00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:22.360
Dell threw pitch after pitch as Daniel stood right behind Patrick.

14
00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:25.759
"Not fast enough, Patrick!" yelled Daniel.

15
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.628
"Too stiff!"

16
00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.996
"Stand higher on your toes!"

17
00:01:29.997 --> 00:01:33.610
Patrick felt stung by his brother's constant criticism.

18
00:01:33.611 --> 00:01:36.443
"What is his problem?" he thought.

19
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:42.030
Mickey returned from his turn in the batting cage and came over to watch Patrick and Dell.

20
00:01:42.031 --> 00:01:49.776
Dell threw a fastball on the outside edge of the plate. Patrick reached for it but missed.

21
00:01:49.777 --> 00:01:53.329
"You should have had that one!" yelled Daniel.

22
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.866
Patrick glared at him, even more embarrassed now that Mickey was watching.

23
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:03.594
He threw the ball back to Dell and then glanced at the bleachers, where his father sat watching practice.

24
00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:08.197
Dad shrugged, signaling to Patrick that everybody misses sometimes.

25
00:02:08.198 --> 00:02:15.739
"Patrick! Keep your head in the game!" Daniel snapped. "Eyes on the field, not the bleachers!"

26
00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.201
"Got it," muttered Patrick.

27
00:02:18.202 --> 00:02:22.162
Finally Coach called Patrick and Dell over to the batting cage.

28
00:02:22.163 --> 00:02:28.922
Mickey and Jerry, a relief pitcher, moved to home plate to work with Daniel.

29
00:02:28.923 --> 00:02:34.064
Dell went into the batting cage first.

30
00:02:34.065 --> 00:02:38.554
Patrick wanted to watch Mickey catch, to assess the other catcher's skills.

31
00:02:38.555 --> 00:02:43.244
But he forced himself to pay attention to Coach's batting instructions instead.

32
00:02:43.245 --> 00:02:48.653
Patrick was too light to have a power swing, so he needed to master the mechanics of batting.

33
00:02:48.654 --> 00:02:56.042
Coach guided Dell into position. "It's one hundred percent physics, plus ten percent attitude," he said.

34
00:02:56.043 --> 00:03:00.185
Patrick and a few other players groaned at Coach's lame joke.

35
00:03:00.186 --> 00:03:06.302
Todd stepped closer to Patrick. "Did you see that new kid hit?"

36
00:03:06.303 --> 00:03:11.767
"Nope." Patrick shook his head, keeping his eyes on Dell. "Is he any good?"

37
00:03:11.768 --> 00:03:20.101
"Unbelievable! He whacked that ball like he was shooting for the moon. He'll be a pinch hitter for sure."

38
00:03:20.102 --> 00:03:25.854
"We'll need a new pinch hitter if you start in left field, Todd," said Buck, their first baseman.

39
00:03:25.855 --> 00:03:30.026
Todd nodded. "Mickey could definitely get the job."

40
00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:36.032
Patrick groaned inwardly. In baseball a pinch hitter came in to hit for another batter.

41
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.142
The player he replaced was out for the rest of the game.

42
00:03:39.143 --> 00:03:44.618
So if Mickey was called in to pinch hit for somebody, Mickey would replace Patrick as catcher.

43
00:03:44.619 --> 00:03:48.426
A few minutes later, it was Patrick's turn in the batting cage.

44
00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:55.075
He set his feet, relaxed into position, and nodded. He was ready for the machine to release a pitch.

45
00:03:55.076 --> 00:03:56.717
Swoosh!

46
00:03:56.718 --> 00:04:01.431
The ball sailed past Patrick and slammed into the net.

47
00:04:01.432 --> 00:04:06.635
"We'll try another one. But first . . ."

48
00:04:06.636 --> 00:04:11.259
Coach came over to adjust Patrick's forward arm and then stepped back.

49
00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:15.080
Ping! This time Patrick tipped the ball.

50
00:04:15.081 --> 00:04:20.737
Whack! The next time he had a solid hit. It was at least a single.

51
00:04:20.738 --> 00:04:24.972
Coach watched Patrick hit a few more times.

52
00:04:24.973 --> 00:04:30.980
"Not bad, Patrick. You're meeting the ball. Spend some time on the weights, building up your strength.

53
00:04:30.981 --> 00:04:34.631
We need to get a few doubles out of you. Next up!"

54
00:04:34.632 --> 00:04:39.709
Patrick left the cage and glanced at home plate, where Daniel was still working with Mickey.

55
00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.383
Patrick tried to read Daniel's expression. Daniel looked . . .

56
00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:47.208
"Impressed," thought Patrick.

57
00:04:47.209 --> 00:04:53.432
"You've got good speed and good instincts, Mickey," Daniel said. "And you know how to use them."

58
00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:59.453
Dell was also watching Daniel and Mickey. "Don't sweat it, Patrick," he said quietly.

59
00:04:59.454 --> 00:05:04.944
"Mickey's good, but he's new, and he's gonna need time to get used to working with our team.

60
00:05:04.945 --> 00:05:10.362
I think Coach will start you—he's seen you play. Plus, you're Daniel's brother."

61
00:05:10.363 --> 00:05:13.293
Patrick nodded, but his throat felt tight.

62
00:05:13.294 --> 00:05:18.004
He was worried about Mickey, and he didn't like being linked to Daniel all the time.

63
00:05:18.005 --> 00:05:20.921
"We'll see," he said with a shrug.

64
00:05:20.922 --> 00:05:28.682
An hour later parents started arriving to pick up their kids. Coach called the team into the dugout before ending practice.

65
00:05:28.683 --> 00:05:34.005
"Good start, boys." He looked down the line of players, meeting each of their eyes.

66
00:05:34.006 --> 00:05:38.835
"How many of you have homework this weekend?" Everyone raised a hand.

67
00:05:38.836 --> 00:05:46.334
"Get it done. Having baseball practice is no excuse for slacking on grades. See you on Monday after school."

68
00:05:46.335 --> 00:05:51.616
Patrick walked out of the dugout with Dell and Daniel.

69
00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:56.822
Mr. Deboe climbed down from the bleachers to join them.

70
00:05:56.823 --> 00:06:00.232
"What did you think of the new kid, Dad?" Daniel asked.

71
00:06:00.233 --> 00:06:04.164
"He looks confident behind the plate," said Mr. Deboe.

72
00:06:04.165 --> 00:06:08.478
"Yeah," agreed Daniel. "He's got sharp instincts."

73
00:06:08.479 --> 00:06:11.129
"Good," said Mr. Deboe.

74
00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:16.357
Patrick trailed behind them into the parking lot.

75
00:06:16.358 --> 00:06:18.957
"What about me?" he thought.

76
00:06:18.958 --> 00:06:24.550
Weren't his dad and brother concerned that Patrick would probably lose his position as starter?

77
00:06:24.551 --> 00:06:33.536
Just then a horn beeped, and Patrick looked up. An old van painted to look like a giant dog sat in the parking lot.

78
00:06:33.537 --> 00:06:38.533
It had eyes and ears sticking up on top and a tongue lapping over the grille.

79
00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:43.134
To Patrick's horror, his mom stepped out of the driver's door.

80
00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:53.351
"Hi, everybody!" she said, a big smile spreading across her freckled face. "Do you like my new van?"

81
00:06:53.352 --> 00:06:58.175
"What?" Patrick thought. "You've got to be kidding me!"

82
00:06:58.176 --> 00:07:03.505
He'd known Mom was buying a van for her new dog-grooming business, Doggie Express.

83
00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:07.256
But he had never imagined it would look like a clown mobile!

84
00:07:07.257 --> 00:07:14.430
Some kids and parents walked over, and Mrs. Deboe started handing out business cards.

85
00:07:14.431 --> 00:07:17.334
A few players were laughing at the van.

86
00:07:17.335 --> 00:07:23.407
"Your doggie van is awesome, Mrs. Deboe!" called Dell. "Woof! Woof!"

87
00:07:23.408 --> 00:07:31.576
"A-roo!" Todd and Buck chimed in, howling and making loud yipping sounds. "Yip, yip, yip!"

88
00:07:31.577 --> 00:07:39.330
Dad and Mom were laughing, but Patrick groaned. "Do I really have to ride around in that thing?"

89
00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:48.317
"Yes," his parents answered. "You do."
